    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> on reaction with excess of water results into acidic mixture&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> is required for the complete neutralisation of the resultant acidic mixture. The number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> used is"
  },
